  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 列\ntitle: row; queue\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 6\nradical: 刀\nradicalNumber: 18\nonyomi: [レツ, レ]\nkunyomi: []\ndistractors: [判, 利, 到]\n---\n\n# 列 — row; queue\n\n**Strokes:** 6 · **Key (radical):** 刀 (as 刂, no. 18) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n列 is an ordered line or row of people or things. The standalone noun [列](../words/列.md) れつ\ncan name a queue, while 列車 れっしゃ names a train.\nThe \"file\" sense in dictionary glosses means a line of people or things, not a computer document.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** use the two upright strokes of 刂 as the straight edge along which a\nqueue lines up. This is a modern visual association, not the character's historical derivation.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe table selects レツ; metadata also preserves レ.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| レツ | on | [列](../words/列.md) れつ — row; 行列 ぎょうれつ — queue |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [列](../words/列.md) れつ — row; line; queue\n- 行列 ぎょうれつ — queue; procession\n- 列車 れっしゃ — train\n\n## Notes\n\n列車 is read れっしゃ, not れつしゃ: learn the small っ as part of the word.\n[判](判.md), [利](利.md), and [到](到.md) also end in 刂.\nTheir shared radical is a visual clue, not a reason to treat their meanings as interchangeable.\n",
